<title>USA: Star to shut Texas hydrocracker Saturday.</title>
<headline>Star to shut Texas hydrocracker Saturday.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Star Enterprise said Friday it would shut a 15,000 barrel per day hydrocracker at its 235,000 bpd refinery in Port Arthur, Texas, for an unplanned repair.</p>
<p>&quot;We're shutting down the hydrocracker to do some unscheduled repair, which means we will be making more heating oil and distillates, which is what we probably should be doing anyway,&quot; said Mike Killien, manager of the refinery.</p>
</text>
